#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:5
#: 1330ff101c7a4d2ab705ce03e8780019
msgid "Setting up the Build Environment on Windows 11 using WSL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:7
#: b261e4970ad14bb59a1be50e66ef08e8
msgid "These setup instructions describe how to set up \"Windows Subsystem for Linux\" for Windows 11  which allows building with waf."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:9
#: d6a3d36d26b64188b360442e3e5479ca
msgid "It involves enabling the built-in Windows Linux environment (WSL) in Windows, installing a compatible Linux distribution, and finally installing the ArduPilot build environment as if it were a normal Linux system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:11
#: 880dbf17fbc84a608a4bd6c3bb97e8ed
msgid "Upon completion, you will be able to build ArduPilot binaries and run the native ArduPilot SITL simulator, including the MAVProxy developer Ground Control Station. You will also be able to use the majority of Linux development features such as debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:14
#: 18d225156fee47fab7acacd086c213cc
msgid "WSL Setup Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:16
#: 1dacbd4ca5f9414ea8298d08d8806b08
msgid "The official instructions are `here <https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:18
#: 4fb684adfec6426e97933ec5c443a8b2
msgid "From the Start menu, start the \"Ubuntu\" application and then follow the :ref:`Ubuntu instructions to install ArduPilot development environment <building-setup-linux>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:20
#: b303b9d74cb64a7d889ce0cb84f80743
msgid "Compilation speeds will be much faster if the ArduPilot repository is downloaded inside of WSL's file system and not externally in the normal Windows file structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:22
#: d3a595b061404e95be7359752a4d8e0b
msgid "To reload the path variables in WSL either close the terminal and reopen it or use: ``logout``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:24
#: 23041561b6bc41d380d5e2d7b399e337
msgid "Windows 11 WSL2 includes a graphical interface for Linux programs. Programs such as ``gedit`` and ``retext`` editors, ``nautilus`` file manager, etc do not need anything additional installed to display graphical interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:26
#: b4759b43c70f443b8a47ebe1816c01d7
msgid "If USB connectivity from within WSL2 is desired, `install USBIPD <https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/connect-usb>`__ or use its GUI application, `WSL USB Manager <https://gitlab.com/alelec/wsl-usb-gui/-/blob/main/README.md>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:29
#: 8afd1be41ea249edbf3d040496b61cfe
msgid "File System Access between WSL and Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:31
#: 8c58d58431cb42cfb14ce75a2d6ea400
msgid "In Windows 11, Windows Explorer will show the file base directory for the Linux system (normally Ubuntu) in its left pane for easy access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:33
#: 1063e3098a3f499aba6b43be877c17db
msgid "Windows files can be from within WSL2 using a file explorer such as ``nautilus`` as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:38
#: d25283f0c7fd433b93139a8d1e5659f4
msgid "Uploading to a board using WSL2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:40
#: 8029b24d64f64f20b0f3426cefa0aaa9
msgid "Uploading to boards (e.g. ``./waf plane --upload``) in WSL2 is possible; however, an installation of Python must exist on the Windows side. Install these packages in Windows Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:46
#: 377655ed2f954c1c8f68b296d8f156c6
msgid "As of July 2022, Microsoft's solution of providing USB access to WSL2 via usbipd does not work for accessing the bootloader on the device due to slow mounting times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:48
#: 228b8aa92dfc4d9c9eb14795efb1c027
msgid "WSL1 can upload to boards by default with no additional changes. This is due to differences in how USB devices are handled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:51
#: 2ac7f5b85e984b3a9712a0cdc198ac8b
msgid "Code Editing in WSL Using VSCode (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:53
#: bc4a9c10234a4895989d37014ea57ac9
msgid "VSCode can be installed on the Windows machine to edit and compile files inside of WSL. VSCode automatically integrates upon installation with WSL. More details are available :ref:`here<editing-the-code-with-vscode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:55
#: f16afb73914c4694873379e1582f2e29
msgid "Do not install VSCode inside of WSL using, for example, apt-get."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:56
#: b41c860fe4bf426c889de5e333117762
msgid "Be sure that the folder you are working on is opened within the WSL remote. This can be achieved by clicking the green button in the bottom left corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:60
#: e4fc8313271140d09d62e3878850e80e
msgid "Windows Terminal (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:62
#: bf55c620a34a4856b0331a5b3d09c80a
msgid "Windows Terminal enables multiple tabs that can switch between many Linux terminals, PowerShell, and more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:64
#: 4444321617cd4f199e6d2d56c1b754d9
msgid "You can change the default terminal when opening Windows Terminal by going to \"Settings\" and moving the Ubuntu section to be first in the ``list`` section of the ``settings.json`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:65
#: 19e0b10b00bf40c58345faa8b9b5b7a2
msgid "The default starting directory can be changed by adding the ``startingDirectory`` line below to your preferred location by following the example below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:66
#: 9ef6bdb04047429989af97c49ed969cb
msgid "Note a similar code block to the one shown below will be automatically generated based upon the version and distribution of Linux installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:80
#: 12a3febff42449c6b78c356c1af23676
msgid "Git Integration with Windows Credential Manager (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-setup-windows11.rst:82
#: 49266c0d58444b4ca3cf784457ad7bce
msgid "Git's Credential Manager can be connected to Window's Credential Manager tokens. This connection prevents re-authentication requests when accessing remote repositories such as GitHub after closing WSL or restarting Windows. The first time a Git operation requires credentials a dialog box will appear automatically to enter your credentials. See this `guide <https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/tutorials/wsl-git#git-credential-manager-setup>`_ for more information regarding GIT and WSL."
msgstr ""
